  "title": { "en": "Hobbies and free time", "uz": "Xobbi va bo'sh vaqt", "ru": "Хобби и свободное время", "tr": "Hobiler ve boş zaman" },
  "goal": {
    "en": "Talk about your hobbies and say what you can and can't do.",
    "uz": "Xobbilaringiz haqida gapiring, nima qila olishingiz va nima qila olmasligingizni ayting.",
    "ru": "Расскажите о своих хобби и о том, что вы умеете и не умеете делать.",
    "tr": "Hobilerinden bahset, neleri yapabildiğini ve neleri yapamadığını söyle."
  },
  "guide": "lumi",
  "color": "#22C55E",
  "tip": {
    "title": { "en": "like + -ing, can / can't", "uz": "like + -ing, can / can't", "ru": "like + -ing, can / can't", "tr": "like + -ing, can / can't" },
    "body": {
      "en": "After like, love and don't like, add -ing to the verb: I like swimming. She likes dancing. To say what you are able to do, put \"can\" before the verb. \"Can\" never changes: no -s and no \"to\": She can swim. For \"no\" say can't: I can't dance. For a question, put \"can\" first: Can you sing?",
      "uz": "like, love, don't like dan keyin fe'lga -ing qo'shiladi: I like swimming (suzishni yoqtiraman). O'zbek tilidagi \"-a olmoq\" (suza olaman) ingliz tilida alohida so'z bilan aytiladi: \"can\" fe'ldan oldin turadi: I can swim. \"Can\" hech qachon o'zgarmaydi, unga -s ham, \"to\" ham qo'shilmaydi: She can swim. Inkor shakli can't: I can't dance. Savolda \"can\" oldinga chiqadi: Can you sing?",
      "ru": "После like, love, don't like к глаголу добавляется -ing: I like swimming (мне нравится плавать). \"Can\" значит «уметь, мочь» и стоит перед глаголом. В отличие от русского, \"can\" не меняется по лицам: без -s и без \"to\": She can swim. Отрицание — can't: I can't dance. В вопросе \"can\" ставится первым: Can you sing?",
      "tr": "like, love, don't like'tan sonra fiile -ing eklenir: I like swimming (yüzmeyi severim). Türkçedeki \"-ebilmek\" eki İngilizcede ayrı bir kelimedir: \"can\" fiilden önce gelir: I can swim. \"Can\" hiç değişmez; -s ya da \"to\" almaz: She can swim. Olumsuzu can't: I can't dance. Soruda \"can\" başa gelir: Can you sing?"
    },
    "examples": [
      { "en": "I like swimming.", "native": { "uz": "Men suzishni yoqtiraman.", "ru": "Мне нравится плавать.", "tr": "Yüzmeyi severim." } },
      { "en": "She can play the guitar.", "native": { "uz": "U gitara chala oladi.", "ru": "Она умеет играть на гитаре.", "tr": "O gitar çalabilir." } },
      { "en": "I can't dance.", "native": { "uz": "Men raqsga tusha olmayman.", "ru": "Я не умею танцевать.", "tr": "Ben dans edemem." } }
    ]
  },
